# GroveSpec's own files stay in git even when the project's .gitignore was written
# for its stack: .NET's `bin/` swallowed .grovespec/bin (a fresh clone then had no
# runtime) and a blanket `*.log` swallowed every review test log (the gate's evidence
# never reached history) — and validate passed throughout, reading the files on disk.
#
# This lives INSIDE the bundle on purpose, like .gitattributes beside it: copying
# .grovespec/ into a project carries the rule along, so the install never edits that
# project's own root .gitignore. A nested file outranks the root one (gitignore(5):
# patterns in a lower-level file override higher-level ones), so `!` re-includes here.
# A project rule that ignores .grovespec/ itself can't be undone from inside it —
# `grovespec validate` names any GroveSpec file git still ignores.
!bin/
!review/*.log
